From 8b02211a8fe39cf1490a78bfe5c71b08c39337d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minhmc2007 <quangminh21072010@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:40:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] mesa-tools: link libxml2.so.2 for the bundled libLLVM

root/bin/mesa_clc: error while loading shared libraries:
libxml2.so.2: cannot open shared object file

The bundled root/lib64/libLLVM.so.20.1 is linked against libxml2.so.2, the
soname of libxml2 2.9. This prebuilt ships no libxml2 in root/lib64, and the
wrapper puts only that directory on LD_LIBRARY_PATH, so it has to resolve from
the host. The host has libxml2 2.15, whose soname is libxml2.so.16, so nothing
resolves.

Symlink the newer soname to the old name. The wrapper only SHA-256 verifies
files that have a .sha256 beside them and this has none, so the symlink is
neither verified nor clobbered.

This is a soname alias, not the library LLVM 20 was built against. Any mesa path
needing an ABI libxml2 2.9 symbol would fail, and the real fix would be to
bundle libxml2.so.2 here. mesa_clc loads and runs with it; it warns "no version
information available" and reaches its argument parser.
---
 root/lib64/libxml2.so.2 | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
 create mode 120000 root/lib64/libxml2.so.2

diff --git a/root/lib64/libxml2.so.2 b/root/lib64/libxml2.so.2
new file mode 120000
index 0000000..8dbab37
--- /dev/null
+++ b/root/lib64/libxml2.so.2
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+/usr/lib/libxml2.so.16
\ No newline at end of file
